# Prompt form of the stinking cloud check (bd inc-uprr): the loaded elf mage
# paints three "stinking cloud" squares east of himself, reads his Fortitude
# bonus off the character sheet, then steps in. The step from plain floor into
# the cloud asks "Confirm enter the stinking cloud?" only when the terrain's
# EV_MON_CONSIDER handler (lib/dungeon.irh) returns ABORT. Read the result with
# tools/check_stinking_cloud_prompt.sh. The step is photographed as @dump:entry
# BEFORE any answer; the script then answers y if asked, steps once more so
# the square he leaves rolls a save (logs/chance_probe.log) -- proof he
# really stood in the cloud -- and walks back.
SPACE
# Farthest square first: a painted square obscures sight, and the cursor
# cannot land on a square the player cannot see.
w
@choose "Change terrain type"
RIGHT RIGHT RIGHT ENTER
TAB
@choose "stinking cloud"
w
@choose "Change terrain type"
RIGHT RIGHT ENTER
TAB
@choose "stinking cloud"
w
@choose "Change terrain type"
RIGHT ENTER
TAB
@choose "stinking cloud"
@dump:terrain-made


d               # Display Character Sheet
@expect "Gender"
@dump:sheet
ESC

RIGHT
@dump:entry
@while "Confirm" y
@dump:entry-after
RIGHT
@while "Confirm" y
LEFT*2
@while "Confirm" y
@dump:walked
@quit
